---
import { cachingProducts } from '../../lib/explainers/caching-model.mjs';
---
<caching-lab class="lab wide" aria-label="Reuse a catalogue response">
 <div class="lab-heading"><span class="eyebrow">Interactive experiment</span><span class="lab-number">01</span></div>
 <h3>How long does the old price stay?</h3>
 <div class="lab-introduction"><p>Three products live in a catalogue. The cache holds two responses, initially none. Each read uses a live copy or fetches the current catalogue value. One time step represents an invented unit of time.</p><p class="try-this">Read the mug twice. Turn off <strong>Invalidate on write</strong>, change its price and stock, then read it again. Advance time until the copy expires and compare the next read. Reading all three products also forces an eviction.</p></div>
 <div class="lab-controls"><p class="lab-area-label">Controls</p>
  <div class="control-line"><label>Product <select data-product>{cachingProducts.map(p=><option value={p.id}>{p.name}</option>)}</select></label><button data-action="read">Read product</button></div>
  <div class="control-line"><label>TTL for new copies <select data-ttl><option value="2">2 steps</option><option value="5" selected>5 steps</option><option value="10">10 steps</option></select></label><label><input data-invalidate type="checkbox" checked /> Invalidate on write</label></div>
  <div class="control-line"><button data-action="write">Change mug price &amp; stock</button><button data-action="tick">Advance time +1</button></div>
  <div class="control-line"><button data-action="outage">Make cache unavailable</button><button data-action="restart">Restart cache empty</button><button data-action="reset">Reset</button></div>
 </div>
 <div class="lab-output paper-surface"><p class="lab-area-label">Result <span>Catalogue, copies, and the last response</span></p><div class="lab-stats" data-stats></div><div class="caching-shelves" data-shelves></div><p class="lab-explanation" data-message role="status" aria-live="polite" aria-atomic="true"></p></div>
 <details class="model-note"><summary>What this model leaves out</summary><p>Requests and writes finish sequentially. The catalogue always succeeds. Copies have fixed expiry from insertion, reads do not renew it, and eviction uses exact least recently used order. Redis and Valkey offer several policies and approximate LRU. This model does not simulate concurrent fills, network delays, persistence, replication, checkout transactions, or measured speed.</p></details>
 <noscript><p>JavaScript enables the controls. A repeated read uses the saved copy; a write without invalidation leaves it stale until expiry. Restarting empty requires fresh catalogue reads.</p></noscript>
</caching-lab>
<script>
 import { createCachingState, cachingStep } from '../../lib/explainers/caching-model.mjs';
 class CachingLab extends HTMLElement {
  connectedCallback() {
   let state = createCachingState();
   const draw = () => {
    this.querySelector('[data-stats]')!.innerHTML = `<div><strong>${state.time}</strong><span>Logical time</span></div><div><strong>${state.reads}</strong><span>Catalogue reads</span></div><div><strong>${state.hits}</strong><span>Cache hits</span></div>`;
    const value = (p:any) => `€${p.price} · stock ${p.stock} · v${p.version}`;
    this.querySelector('[data-shelves]')!.innerHTML = `<div><h4>Authoritative catalogue</h4>${state.source.map((p:any)=>`<p><b>${p.name}</b><span>${value(p)}</span></p>`).join('')}</div><div><h4>Cache: ${state.available?'reachable':'unavailable'}</h4>${state.entries.length?state.entries.map((e:any)=>`<p class="${e.value.version!==state.source.find((p:any)=>p.id===e.id)?.version?'caching-stale':''}"><b>${e.value.name}</b><span>${value(e.value)}</span><small>Expires at ${e.expires} · ${e.expires-state.time} steps left</small></p>`).join(''):'<p>No copies</p>'}</div><div><h4>Last response</h4>${state.last?`<p><b>${state.last.name}</b><span>${value(state.last)}</span><small>From ${state.last.from} at time ${state.last.at}</small></p>`:'<p>No request yet</p>'}</div>`;
    this.querySelector('[data-message]')!.textContent=state.message;
    this.querySelector('[data-action="outage"]')!.textContent=state.available?'Make cache unavailable':'Restore cache';
   };
   this.addEventListener('click',event=>{
    const button=(event.target as HTMLElement).closest<HTMLButtonElement>('button[data-action]'); if(!button)return;
    const type=button.dataset.action;
    if(type==='reset'){state=createCachingState(); (this.querySelector('[data-product]') as HTMLSelectElement).value='mug'; (this.querySelector('[data-ttl]') as HTMLSelectElement).value='5'; (this.querySelector('[data-invalidate]') as HTMLInputElement).checked=true;}
    else state=cachingStep(state,{type,id:(this.querySelector('[data-product]') as HTMLSelectElement).value}); draw();
   });
   this.querySelector('[data-ttl]')!.addEventListener('change',event=>{state=cachingStep(state,{type:'ttl',value:(event.target as HTMLSelectElement).value});draw();});
   this.querySelector('[data-invalidate]')!.addEventListener('change',event=>{state=cachingStep(state,{type:'invalidation',value:(event.target as HTMLInputElement).checked});draw();});
   draw();
  }
 }
 if(!customElements.get('caching-lab'))customElements.define('caching-lab',CachingLab);
</script>
<style>
 .caching-shelves { display:grid; grid-template-columns:repeat(3,minmax(0,1fr)); gap:1.2rem; margin:1.4rem 0; }
 .caching-shelves > div { min-width:0; border-top:1px solid var(--color-rule-strong); }
 .caching-shelves h4 {font-size:.85rem; margin:.7rem 0;}
 .caching-shelves :global(p) {padding:.6rem 0;border-bottom:1px solid var(--color-rule);font-size:.8rem;line-height:1.6;}
 .caching-shelves :global(b),.caching-shelves :global(span),.caching-shelves :global(small){display:block;}
 .caching-shelves :global(.caching-stale){border-left:3px solid var(--coral);padding-left:.5rem;}
 @media(max-width:650px){.caching-shelves{grid-template-columns:1fr;gap:.5rem;}}
</style>
